# What has each metric read for this endpoint, across every run in the store?
#
# The page this feeds answers the question the name of this project makes: not
# "is it up" but "has it changed". Every other read query here is about ONE run,
# the newest that measured an endpoint, and deliberately so; this one is about
# all of them and is the only query that crosses run graphs on purpose.
#
# ?endpoint is the input, substituted as a NamedNode (SEP-0007), which is why it
# appears in the projection: pyoxigraph substitutes projected variables only.
#
# NO `urn:sparqlwatch:current` HERE, unlike every other query in this
# directory. current names the newest run per endpoint, and a history that read
# it would be a history of one run. The run graphs are the record and they are
# never rewritten, so walking them IS the history.
#
# ORDERED BY THE RUN'S OWN TIMESTAMP, not by the run IRI. The IRI happens to
# contain an ISO instant today and sorting on it would work by accident; a run
# named any other way would silently reorder the history, and a reordered
# history reads as an endpoint that recovered when it broke.
#
# ONE ROW PER (run, metric) THAT SAID SOMETHING, and no row where a run said
# nothing. A run that predates a metric has no fact about it, and neither does a
# run whose sweep never reached it. Both are absences the CALLER renders as a
# gap, which is the same reading the index gives an empty cell: this run
# recorded nothing about that metric, which is not a verdict about the endpoint.
#
# A DECLINE IS A ROW, with ?reason bound and ?verdict unbound. "We chose not to
# look" is something a run said, and drawing it as a gap would lose the
# difference between a sweep that declined a metric and a sweep that had never
# heard of it.

PREFIX dqv: <http://www.w3.org/ns/dqv#>
PREFIX prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#>
PREFIX sw: <urn:sparqlwatch:>

SELECT ?endpoint ?run ?generatedAt ?metric ?verdict ?reason
WHERE {
  GRAPH ?run {
    ?activity a prov:Activity ;
              prov:generatedAtTime ?generatedAt .
    {
      ?measurement dqv:computedOn ?endpoint ;
                   dqv:isMeasurementOf ?metric ;
                   dqv:value ?verdict .
    }
    UNION
    {
      ?notMeasured sw:notMeasuredOn ?endpoint ;
                   sw:notMeasuredMetric ?metric ;
                   sw:notMeasuredReason ?reason .
    }
  }
}
ORDER BY ?generatedAt ?metric
